            <ArticleTitle>Synthesis and SAR of 4-carboxy-2-azetidinone mechanism-based tryptase inhibitors.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>3229-33</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A series of N1-activated C4-carboxy azetidinones was prepared and tested as inhibitors of human tryptase. The key stereochemical and functional features required for potency, serine protease specificity and aqueous stability were determined. From these studies compound 2, BMS-262084, was identified as a potent and selective tryptase inhibitor which, when dosed intratracheally in ovalbumin-sensitized guinea pigs, reduced allergen-induced bronchoconstriction and inflammatory cell infiltration into the lung.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
